<h5><code>Link Updates</code></h5>

<p>
  The server sends this payload immediately after subscribing and every time client-visible link state changes. Treat
  <code>post_url</code> as the current wallpaper URL. Users can enable videos and GIFs on some links, so clients should
  handle file types they cannot display.
</p>

<div class="accent-block">
  <div class="accent-block__charm">
    <ion-icon role="presentation" name="arrow-down-circle"></ion-icon>
    Message
  </div>
  <pre><code class="language-json">{
  "success": true,
  "id": 1,
  "expires": "2026-03-05T00:00:00.000Z",
  "username": "gray",
  "terms": "I'm trying out something new, break this please! :)",
  "blacklist": "feet blood",
  "post_url": "https://static1.e621.net/data/5d/87/5d87428c4839b0dc7d585b87a25af61a.png",
  "post_thumbnail_url": "https://static1.e621.net/data/preview/5d/87/5d87428c4839b0dc7d585b87a25af61a.jpg",
  "post_description": "",
  "created_at": "2022-03-08T01:01:50.142Z",
  "updated_at": "2022-03-13T21:39:01.828Z",
  "set_by": "name",
  "response_type": "horny",
  "response_text": "HUFF wow",
  "online": true
}</code></pre>
</div>

<p>
  If the link does not exist, the channel sends an error payload and does not stream link updates.
</p>

<div class="accent-block">
  <div class="accent-block__charm">
    <ion-icon role="presentation" name="warning"></ion-icon>
    Error
  </div>
  <pre><code class="language-json">{
  "success": false,
  "why": "Link 0 does not exist."
}</code></pre>
</div>

